{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"U-وجد\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The two uses of وَجَدَ in 18:86 shift from perceiving the sun in a setting state (وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ) to encountering people at the scene (وَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًا). 3:37 repeats وَجَدَ عِندَهَا for provision found with Maryam, supporting a locative discovery pattern.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَوَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"3:37\",\"ar\":\"كُلَّمَا دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا زَكَرِيَّا ٱلْمِحْرَابَ وَجَدَ عِندَهَا رِزْقًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated verb takes different complements in 18:86, and its second use shares the عِندَهَا construction with 3:37.\",\"limits\":\"The parallel supports a locative discovery pattern; it does not settle the referent of ها in 18:86 or equate the people with the provision.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"U-عين\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ identifies a spring or source, while 18:28 and 18:101 use the same root for eyes. Together with وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ, those same-surah eye uses may lend the scene a visual undertone.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:28\",\"ar\":\"وَلَا تَعْدُ عَيْنَاكَ عَنْهُمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:101\",\"ar\":\"كَانَتْ أَعْيُنُهُمْ فِى غِطَآءٍ عَن ذِكْرِى\"}],\"missing\":\"These passages establish the root's eye sense elsewhere in the surah, but not simultaneous wordplay in 18:86. A lexicon describing an eye or aperture extension in the spring sense, or a Quranic parallel that joins eye and spring imagery, could strengthen the link.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"U-حمء\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The three other occurrences are noun حَمَإٍ in one repeated creation passage, while 18:86 uniquely uses adjective حَمِئَةٍ for the spring. This may give the muddy setting a material echo of human origins as the verse turns to قَوْمًا, but the shared root alone leaves that link uncertain.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ وَوَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"15:26\",\"ar\":\"خَلَقْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ مِن صَلْصَٰلٍۢ مِّنْ حَمَإٍۢ مَّسْنُونٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"15:28\",\"ar\":\"خَٰلِقٌۢ بَشَرًۭا مِّن صَلْصَٰلٍۢ مِّنْ حَمَإٍۢ مَّسْنُونٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"15:33\",\"ar\":\"بَشَرٍ خَلَقْتَهُۥ مِن صَلْصَٰلٍۢ مِّنْ حَمَإٍۢ مَّسْنُونٍۢ\"}],\"missing\":\"The creation passage and the spring scene share the root but differ in form and context. A direct textual echo between them, or lexical evidence clarifying whether حَمِئَةٍ carries the creation-mud sense as well as describing a muddy spring, could establish whether the association is intended.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
